  title = {Kant on Marriage},
  publisher = {Cambridge University Press},
  year = {2025},
  doi = {10.1017/9781009304559},
  note = {SUMMARY: A Cambridge Element that reconstructs Kant's account of marriage from its context and background conversations and from the conception of equality at its core. That equality does not precede marriage and was inaccessible to much of the German population; the author sets Kant beside the eighteenth-century feminist writers Theodor von Hippel and Marianne Ehrmann and concludes that his conception is compatible with certain egalitarian goals and might improve women's lives in a liberal state (publisher abstract).

